  "questions": [
    {
      "dom_id": "question-181775",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=R\\times R$ in the Cartesian plane?",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=R\\times R\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in R,\\,y\\in R}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}={(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14120023/assets/07a3d9a6c38b5bfcc529496735a1a66eaceefd5ae3437a2cb0cd45911eccafae.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in R$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}={(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in R,$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14120023/assets/e454f1cf125486ca25acf15e26efd251a4a03b08e899814ab3e77db7898713c4.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $R:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in R}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nThis is the whole plane, as shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14120023/assets/070389fcdb6d69f9aa90dabbd98a0d3461e26d3e3e08b1d53b92e99688c09923.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-181775\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">1.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/4387#13320\">Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"181775\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Which of the following is a representation of the set <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"1\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D446 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-texatom space=\"4\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c211D TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-cD7\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-texatom space=\"3\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c211D TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><mo>×</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> in the Cartesian plane?</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Sun, Oct 11th @ 9:23 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 1:57</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>",
